cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Signed multi-interest recommendation"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-31"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/signed-multi-interest-recommender"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/signed-multi-interest-recommender"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research software for explicit-negative ranking on frozen content embeddings.
  Includes SignedMax, linear and kernel baselines, matched controls, temporal
  user-disjoint evaluation, immutable confirmation provenance, paired user
  bootstrap comparisons and CPU cost measurements. On MovieLens 1M with a fixed
  MiniLM encoder, all 13 frozen method slots completed for 1776 confirmation
  users. SignedMax underperformed preselected logistic regression and the
  negative-mean baseline. Published aggregates and a dependency-free checker
  support inspection without distributing dataset contents or model weights.
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - explicit negative feedback
  - content embeddings
  - reproducible research
  - negative results
